{"atom_id": "DOC:newinml2026_successor_v4:ABS-SENT:0", "atom_type": "Sentence", "parent": "DOC:newinml2026_successor_v4", "text": "Agent evaluations increasingly depend on context interventions---retrieval, memory graphs, and prompt contracts---yet published reports often omit null outcomes, parser failures, and negative cells."}
{"atom_id": "DOC:newinml2026_successor_v4:ABS-SENT:1", "atom_type": "Sentence", "parent": "DOC:newinml2026_successor_v4", "text": "We present HydraDG, a governed experimental framework that binds substantive model invocations, tool calls, and handoffs to   (FCOs) and a   (FCG)."}
{"atom_id": "DOC:newinml2026_successor_v4:ABS-SENT:2", "atom_type": "Sentence", "parent": "DOC:newinml2026_successor_v4", "text": "HydraDG preregisters hypotheses, freezes case manifests and scorers, records raw prompt and response hashes, and preserves terminal states including timeouts, abstentions, and malformed outputs without silent substitution."}
{"atom_id": "DOC:newinml2026_successor_v4:ABS-SENT:3", "atom_type": "Sentence", "parent": "DOC:newinml2026_successor_v4", "text": "We report two preregistered studies (EXP-008, EXP-009) comparing flat prose versus structured FCG retrieval for failure-prevention endpoints; both terminate as   under bounded case replication, so confirmatory effect claims are not supported while negative and null evidence remains in custody."}
{"atom_id": "DOC:newinml2026_successor_v4:ABS-SENT:4", "atom_type": "Sentence", "parent": "DOC:newinml2026_successor_v4", "text": "We argue that custody-first evaluation infrastructure supports reproducible agent science rather than optional logging."}
